Only a view that drew is clean, and three numbers that show where a repaint goes.

THE FIX. displayRectIgnoringOpacity: retired a view's dirty rectangles whether or not canDraw had
let drawRect: run. canDraw is NO for a windowless or hidden view, which is exactly the state a view
is in while its tree is being assembled, so a display request arriving then was answered by marking
the view clean and painting nothing. The request was gone and the next pass saw nothing to do.
Retiring is now conditional on canDraw, which is the only reading under which the word clean means
anything.

THE INSTRUMENTS, all on the existing CIDER_TRACE_LAYERBLIT and CIDER_TRACE_DIRTY switches:
  - the view tree dump prints the POINTER and the dirty flag. It named views by class alone, so
    with two instances of a class there was no way to tell whether the view being marked was the
    one in the tree. It is the same view: 0x72a6803b4e20 in both.
  - cider-descent counts the views each display pass walks, so a pass that stops early is a number
    rather than an absence. iTerm2 walks 81 views 20 times out of a tree of exactly 81, which is
    how the raise-unwinds-the-traversal theory died.
  - CIDER_RETIRE names every view marked clean by the rect bookkeeping rather than by a draw, with
    the rectangle drawn and the visible rectangle.

WHAT THEY MEASURED, and it moves task #239 across the boundary. iTerm2 3.5.14 marks its terminal
view 482 times. The traversal visits it every pass. It is retired 8 times with why=covered and
drew=0,0 1241x632 visible=0,0 1241x632, which is the FULL rect with canDraw true, so its drawRect:
ran 8 times. It produced glyphs exactly once: 128 glyph runs at startup and none after.

So the repaint is not being lost on our side. It is delivered, in full, and the application draws
nothing into it. THE canDraw FIX IS NOT THE FIX FOR #239 AND I AM NOT CLAIMING IT IS: measured
before and after, the terminal is still marked 482 times and redrawn once.

